Usage: atc <command> [options]

Atomic Server keeps models on this machine and serves them over an OpenAI-compatible API; atc is its command. Install an engine, pull a model, run it — and manage it all from here, the terminal UI (bare `atc` on a terminal) or the local web admin.

Server:
  control  Typed server operations for scripts and agents
  setup    Plan, apply or skip server setup
  mcp      Serve agent tools over MCP stdio
  start    Start the server (core, API, web admin) in the background
  stop     Stop the server: unload the models, stop the API and the admin
  restart  Stop the server if it runs, then start it
  status   Show the server, the API endpoint, running models and the admin URL
  logs     Show the server log

Models & engines:
  run       Load a downloaded model
  unload    Unload a model; keep its files and server running
  models    Discover, download and manage model files
  engines   Discover and manage engine builds
  hardware  Hardware facts and engine devices

Access:
  connect  Connection details or launch an installed agent
  api      The OpenAI-compatible API and its key
  admin    The web admin: open it, see where it listens, manage its token
  tui      Full-screen terminal UI over the server (what bare `atc` opens on a terminal)
  chat     Send a message to an OpenAI-compatible model

System:
  config      Read and change atc settings
  doctor      Check the installation: folders, config, ports, PATH, GPU, managed engines
  service     Run the server as an OS service (systemd, launchd, Windows task)
  update      Update atc to the latest release
  version     Print the atc, core and admin versions
  completion  Print a shell completion script (bash, zsh, fish, powershell)

Global options:
  --json                Print the result as one JSON document (errors go to stderr as JSON)
  -v, --verbose         Debug-level logging on stderr
  -q, --quiet           Only errors on stderr; no progress
  -y, --yes             Answer yes to safe confirmations; required for elevation and deletion
                        without a terminal
  --data-folder <path>  Data folder to work with (default: <system data>/atomic-chat-cli/data)
  --no-color            Disable ANSI colours (NO_COLOR is honoured too)
  -h, --help            Show help
  --version             Print the version

